   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Communications (Online Advertisement, Newspaper Advertisement, Radio Advertisement and Media Parley)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">We conducted two impactful media parleys: one focused on the state of freedom of expression in Nigeria and NITDA&apos;s code of practice, while the other marked the launch of the Londa report. In addition, our campaign utilized online advertisements, harnessing audiovisual content for widespread promotion across diverse social media platforms including YouTube, Instagram, Facebook, Twitter, and LinkedIn. We extended our reach further through newspaper advertisements, addressing critical issues such as the proposed Social Media bill and advocating against civic restrictions.

Expanding our campaign to radio, we strategically aired informative segments on three prominent Abuja radio stations for a week, rallying support against the anti-social media bill. Moreover, we initiated a dynamic #SayNoToSocialMediaBill radio tour, engaging with audiences across 26 states to emphasize the importance of an approach that respects individual rights when considering legislative proposals. These comprehensive efforts synergistically conveyed our messages and galvanized public support for our cause.</narrative>
   </description>
